CP372 Assignment 2 - Bonus Implementation Note

Our project implements robust packet corruption detection using CRC32 checksums 
via Python's built-in `zlib` library. Every packet header includes a 4-byte 
checksum field (`csum`) calculated over the entire packet structure (type, 
sequence number, acknowledgment number, payload length, and payload data). 

Upon receiving data packets or acknowledgments, both senders and receivers 
re-calculate the CRC32 checksum. If a packet's data is corrupted in transit 
or modified by the simulation loss rate, the checksum verification fails, 
triggering a packet drop / retransmission behavior.
